<%#
  Comments on the file as a whole (GitHub `subjectType: FILE`), at the top
  where they set the frame for reading the rest.

  They have no line, so there is no block to sit under. Prism's own file-level
  fallback — a comment on a block GitHub can't anchor to — lands here too:
  ReviewCommentsController streams it into `#file_threads`. The heading is
  always in the DOM so a first streamed-in thread gets one; `.file-threads`
  hides the whole section while the list is empty.

  Locals: threads ([Github::Types::ReviewThread]), pull_request
%>
<section class="md-row file-threads" aria-labelledby="file-threads-heading">
  <div class="md-gutter" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="md-body">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="file-threads-heading">Comments on this file</h2>
    </div>

    <div id="file_threads" data-testid="file-threads">
      <% threads.each do |thread| %>
        <%= render "thread", thread: thread, pull_request: pull_request, block_id: "file" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
